1
00:00:15,249 --> 00:00:16,457
"You mean The Next Leader?"

2
00:00:16,457 --> 00:00:22,308
"If my team wins, I call the shots on the new president."

3
00:00:22,308 --> 00:00:27,449
"I'm Pong. I heard you're forming a team for The Next Leader?"

4
00:00:27,449 --> 00:00:29,460
"Can I lend a hand?"

5
00:00:29,460 --> 00:00:31,231
"Much safer this way."

6
00:00:31,231 --> 00:00:34,257
"Ya isn't here by choice."

7
00:00:34,257 --> 00:00:38,329
"If her team wins The Next Leader, do you really think she'll stay?"

8
00:00:38,329 --> 00:00:40,538
"So this... is why you've been so nice to me."

9
00:00:40,538 --> 00:00:43,928
"If I were only doing this for my own gain... I wouldn't have gone this far."

10
00:00:43,928 --> 00:00:45,411
"I can't compete for you anymore."

11
00:00:45,411 --> 00:00:48,722
"Actually... you don't need to care so much about Din."

12
00:00:48,722 --> 00:00:50,332
"You still have me."

13
00:00:50,332 --> 00:00:52,646
"I'm here to register for Mr. Ronnayut's team."

14
00:00:52,646 --> 00:00:54,113
"Did you play me?"

15
00:00:54,113 --> 00:00:58,127
"If there are no more teams, I'll be closing the registration."

16
00:01:02,867 --> 00:01:03,541
"Here. And don't tell anyone."

17
00:01:09,533 --> 00:01:10,213
"Oh, hi Ya..."

18
00:01:10,213 --> 00:01:11,889
My girlfriend's in HR. Everyone's talking about it...

19
00:01:11,889 --> 00:01:13,413
My girlfriend's in HR. Everyone's talking about it...

20
00:01:13,413 --> 00:01:17,836
Khun Ya didn't even want to work here. If she wins, do you really think she'll stay?

21
00:01:17,836 --> 00:01:19,296
"Did you lie to me?"

22
00:01:19,296 --> 00:01:21,335
"When did I ever lie to you?"

23
00:01:21,335 --> 00:01:25,025
Don't forget... when I asked to join your team,

24
00:01:25,025 --> 00:01:29,572
weren't you the one who never once accepted me?

25
00:01:29,586 --> 00:01:32,054
So now... what exactly are you talking about, Khun Ya?

26
00:01:33,988 --> 00:01:39,556
"Ah... or did what happened last night... give you the wrong idea?"

27
00:01:39,556 --> 00:01:44,933
If so... then I'm sorry.

28
00:01:48,653 --> 00:01:50,336
"Let me teach you something, Ya...

29
00:01:50,336 --> 00:01:53,327
never trust anyone."

30
00:01:55,611 --> 00:01:58,445
- If there are no other teams, I'll be closing the registration now.

31
00:01:58,445 --> 00:01:59,303
Wait!

32
00:02:02,026 --> 00:02:02,615
"Am I too late?"

33
00:02:02,615 --> 00:02:03,521
"You're just in time."

34
00:02:21,066 --> 00:02:22,853
I'd like to register for The Next Leader...

35
00:02:23,732 --> 00:02:25,073
on behalf of Khun Thanya!

36
00:02:39,147 --> 00:02:41,137
Someone like you wants to compete too?

37
00:02:41,137 --> 00:02:42,251
huh?

38
00:02:43,646 --> 00:02:45,551
"I didn't want to at first...

39
00:02:45,551 --> 00:02:47,420
but I changed my mind."

40
00:02:51,145 --> 00:02:53,276
"Someone as naive and clueless as you...

41
00:02:53,276 --> 00:02:56,180
is going to have a hard time in this world."

42
00:02:57,519 --> 00:02:59,359
Ever heard of 'no pain, no gain'?

43
00:02:59,359 --> 00:03:01,912
I'll see you at the competition...

44
00:03:01,912 --> 00:03:04,221
just don't come begging for help.

45
00:03:07,476 --> 00:03:09,482
P'Din... hurry up and sign it before it's too late.

46
00:03:11,476 --> 00:03:17,503
I'd love to see... what a nobody like you is actually capable of.

47
00:03:20,475 --> 00:03:21,345
What the hell is he going on about?

48
00:03:34,890 --> 00:03:35,971
[Sighs] Thank you so much.

49
00:04:56,337 --> 00:04:57,853
Why did you come back to help me?

50
00:04:59,754 --> 00:05:00,956
Well... it's like this, gorgeous.

51
00:05:00,956 --> 00:05:08,629
Well, our Khun Time here... heard that Khun Ronnayut and P'Pong... want to leave you without a team.

52
00:05:08,629 --> 00:05:11,385
So I... this handsome guy right here...

53
00:05:11,385 --> 00:05:14,425
got P'Time to tell P'Din...

54
00:05:14,425 --> 00:05:16,808
and begged him to come help you.

55
00:05:16,808 --> 00:05:19,895
So basically... I'm the mastermind behind all of this.

56
00:05:19,895 --> 00:05:21,870
- Shh!

57
00:05:21,870 --> 00:05:23,870
-what?!

58
00:05:25,167 --> 00:05:26,838
"I don't like playing dirty."

59
00:05:29,208 --> 00:05:30,547
"Thank you so much...

60
00:05:30,547 --> 00:05:32,851
And thanks to Kanghan and Time, too."

61
00:05:32,851 --> 00:05:34,691
"My pleasure, Miss Ya."

62
00:05:40,165 --> 00:05:41,422
"Don't thank me just yet...

63
00:05:42,623 --> 00:05:43,635
Miss Ya."

64
00:05:52,039 --> 00:05:53,549
"My pleasure... Young Master Time."

65
00:05:54,746 --> 00:05:55,455
"Huh?"

66
00:06:19,702 --> 00:06:20,737
"Who the hell is that kid?"

67
00:06:22,243 --> 00:06:23,210
"Do you mean Din, sir?"

68
00:06:24,743 --> 00:06:28,424
"He's just an ordinary employee...nothing special, and definitely no threat."

69
00:06:29,867 --> 00:06:31,007
"Look into his background...

70
00:06:31,007 --> 00:06:33,321
I want to know who he is."

71
00:06:34,575 --> 00:06:35,405
"Don't let your guard down...

72
00:06:35,405 --> 00:06:39,398
We must win this competition."

73
00:06:41,782 --> 00:06:42,965
"Don't worry, sir...

74
00:06:42,965 --> 00:06:46,280
there's no way that Din guy can beat me."

75
00:06:46,280 --> 00:06:48,367
"Rest assured, sir...

76
00:06:48,367 --> 00:06:52,609
I will definitely win The Next Leader competition."

77
00:06:52,609 --> 00:06:57,742
"But... if I win, you have to..."

78
00:06:57,742 --> 00:06:58,894
"I know!

79
00:06:58,894 --> 00:07:02,388
Once you win, I'll give you a promotion."

80
00:07:19,652 --> 00:07:21,027
"Hey!

81
00:07:21,110 --> 00:07:23,418
You got off work ages ago. What took you so long?"

82
00:07:23,418 --> 00:07:25,522
"Why haven't you gone home yet?"

83
00:07:25,522 --> 00:07:28,353
"Aha! Or could it be...

84
00:07:28,353 --> 00:07:30,900
you're worried about me?"

85
00:07:30,900 --> 00:07:32,543
"Did I say that?

86
00:07:32,543 --> 00:07:33,939
I have no idea what you're talking about."

87
00:07:35,317 --> 00:07:36,684
"Alright, alright... let's go."

88
00:07:37,817 --> 00:07:38,770
"Let's go grab a bite."

89
00:07:40,858 --> 00:07:42,082
"I'm not... free."

90
00:07:44,441 --> 00:07:45,230
"Why?

91
00:07:45,230 --> 00:07:46,295
Where are you going?"

92
00:07:46,295 --> 00:07:48,790
"Let me tag along!"

93
00:07:48,790 --> 00:07:50,646
"Why are you so pushy, huh?!"

94
00:07:52,023 --> 00:07:53,754
"Pleeease... please, please, please!"

95
00:07:53,754 --> 00:07:55,060
just let me come along."

96
00:07:56,481 --> 00:07:58,503
"I promise, once you're done with your errands..

97
00:07:58,503 --> 00:08:03,497
just think about it... I'll take you to a restaurant that meets Young Master Time's standards."

98
00:08:04,771 --> 00:08:06,442
"Stop calling me 'Young Master Time' already."

99
00:08:11,937 --> 00:08:13,363
"Hey! Are you coming or not?"

100
00:08:14,354 --> 00:08:15,009
"You're letting me come?

101
00:08:16,562 --> 00:08:17,600
I'm coming, I'm coming!

102
00:08:17,600 --> 00:08:18,228
Let's go!

103
00:08:18,228 --> 00:08:19,669
Let's go... Young Master Time."

104
00:08:53,140 --> 00:08:55,253
"Working overtime, huh... Young Miss?"

105
00:08:55,253 --> 00:08:58,662
"So you're really not going to drop this, are you?"

106
00:09:01,014 --> 00:09:01,756
"Anyway, what are you up to?"

107
00:09:03,056 --> 00:09:04,851
"I'm prepping for the match, you know."

108
00:09:04,851 --> 00:09:08,922
"Honestly, I barely know anything... about my dad's company."

109
00:09:08,922 --> 00:09:10,379
"I'm glad you're here."

110
00:09:10,379 --> 00:09:12,885
"What's the difference between all these? Show me."

111
00:09:14,387 --> 00:09:15,907
"You've never seen a pipe before or what?"

112
00:09:15,907 --> 00:09:18,060
"Stop teasing me."

113
00:09:18,060 --> 00:09:23,154
"I know they look the same... but they're actually different, right?"

114
00:09:26,094 --> 00:09:27,228
"Alright... check this out."

115
00:09:27,228 --> 00:09:30,046
"What's the difference between these two pipes?"

116
00:09:34,135 --> 00:09:35,875
"They look exactly the same!"

117
00:09:39,176 --> 00:09:42,052
This one's thicker, so it's better quality.

118
00:09:42,052 --> 00:09:43,765
It can handle higher water pressure.

119
00:09:47,508 --> 00:09:48,806
"I can't tell at all."

120
00:09:48,806 --> 00:09:50,653
"Then look a little closer."

121
00:09:54,091 --> 00:09:54,841
"See that?

122
00:09:54,841 --> 00:09:56,427
Now look at this one."

123
00:10:00,382 --> 00:10:03,487
"This one's heavier, which means it has more limestone...

124
00:10:03,487 --> 00:10:05,095
to cut production costs."

125
00:10:05,095 --> 00:10:07,078
"If you actually use this one...

126
00:10:07,078 --> 00:10:10,868
it'll get brittle and break easily."

127
00:10:23,170 --> 00:10:24,130
"What are you smiling at?"

128
00:10:24,130 --> 00:10:27,044
"Well... you seem really eager to learn."

129
00:10:27,044 --> 00:10:30,464
"I just want to learn as much as I can...

130
00:10:30,464 --> 00:10:32,705
so I can actually help you."

131
00:10:35,127 --> 00:10:37,781
"But we don't have this pipe at our company...

132
00:10:37,781 --> 00:10:39,088
where did you get it?"

133
00:10:39,088 --> 00:10:40,951
"I just grabbed it from around here...

134
00:10:40,951 --> 00:10:42,417
I don't know."

135
00:10:42,417 --> 00:10:44,893
"The quality is really bad...

136
00:10:44,893 --> 00:10:45,898
here...

137
00:10:45,898 --> 00:10:47,226
let me show you."

138
00:10:47,226 --> 00:10:52,217
"Not all pipes are the same thickness."

139
00:10:52,217 --> 00:10:54,860
"See for yourself... they're not the same."

140
00:10:57,583 --> 00:11:00,795
"Because the thicker it is, the more water pressure it can handle."

141
00:11:03,873 --> 00:11:05,398
"See? ...This one's thicker."

142
00:11:07,248 --> 00:11:08,349
Din: "What are you doing? ...Are you messing around?"
Ya: (Laughs)

143
00:11:08,349 --> 00:11:10,299
"See? ...This one's thicker."

144
00:11:33,161 --> 00:11:35,270
"How is it? ...Do you like this place?"

145
00:11:35,270 --> 00:11:37,992
"I found a place that's absolutely perfect for you."

146
00:11:39,952 --> 00:11:40,504
"Like it?"

147
00:11:42,243 --> 00:11:43,493
"Yeah!"

148
00:11:44,618 --> 00:11:46,095
"But... why?

149
00:11:46,095 --> 00:11:48,625
Do I seem that high-maintenance?"

150
00:11:48,625 --> 00:11:52,006
"Whoa... come on, you absolutely must have an air-conditioned room."

151
00:11:56,908 --> 00:11:58,939
"Then why did you bring me here?"

152
00:11:58,939 --> 00:12:02,098
"Oh... well, this is my friend's place."

153
00:12:02,098 --> 00:12:03,274
"Ah..."

154
00:12:03,274 --> 00:12:05,990
"Honestly, I can't afford to eat at a place like this every day."

155
00:12:05,990 --> 00:12:08,205
"But the owner is an old friend from school."

156
00:12:08,205 --> 00:12:08,992
"Mhm..."

157
00:12:08,992 --> 00:12:11,020
"So the price is very friend..."

158
00:12:11,020 --> 00:12:11,876
"Fraud!"

159
00:12:11,876 --> 00:12:13,151
"Friendly!

160
00:12:13,151 --> 00:12:15,431
"Fraud is right... I mean you."

161
00:12:15,431 --> 00:12:17,848
"Hey... I went out of my way to bring you here."

162
00:12:27,238 --> 00:12:28,476
"What can I get for you?"

163
00:12:30,945 --> 00:12:32,409
"Order whatever you'd like, Time."

164
00:12:32,409 --> 00:12:33,122
Okay.

165
00:12:33,122 --> 00:12:34,240
"And... this is my friend."

166
00:12:34,240 --> 00:12:36,087
"Oh... nice to meet you."

167
00:12:41,777 --> 00:12:43,828
"Eyebrows send to the eyes... eyes send to the mouth...

168
00:12:43,828 --> 00:12:46,612
mouth sends to the eyes... eyes send to the chin..."

169
00:12:46,612 --> 00:12:47,389
"Hey! Shh, shh, shh!"

170
00:12:47,389 --> 00:12:49,150
"Shh... Louis, keep it down."

171
00:12:49,150 --> 00:12:50,143
"He's super cute... come on!"

172
00:12:50,143 --> 00:12:50,770
"I'll be right back... just a sec."

173
00:12:50,770 --> 00:12:51,716
"I'm Louis,

174
00:12:51,716 --> 00:12:52,670
by the way... and I'm single."

175
00:12:52,670 --> 00:12:54,129
"Louis... get over there... Louis!"

176
00:12:54,129 --> 00:12:56,069
Louis: "If you want to know about him... I'll tell you."
Kangkhan: "Shh! Shhh!"

177
00:12:56,069 --> 00:12:57,363
"Why are you bringing up old stuff...?"

178
00:12:58,984 --> 00:12:59,775
"Why not?"

179
00:13:00,442 --> 00:13:01,444
"He's super cute...

180
00:13:02,858 --> 00:13:03,700
are you getting jealous?"

181
00:13:03,700 --> 00:13:04,797
"So, what are you two...

182
00:13:05,774 --> 00:13:06,567
what's the deal here?"

183
00:13:07,774 --> 00:13:10,759
"We're not anything... he's just like a brother to me."

184
00:13:10,759 --> 00:13:13,177
"If you're just brothers... then he's fair game."

185
00:13:13,177 --> 00:13:14,367
"Hey... excuse me..."

186
00:13:14,367 --> 00:13:15,876
"Like hell you can! Hey, cut it out! Listen to me!"

187
00:13:15,876 --> 00:13:18,046
"You're talking way too much... Why are you so talkative today?"

188
00:13:18,046 --> 00:13:19,439
"Are you screwing with me right now?"

189
00:13:19,439 --> 00:13:22,578
"And stop coming over to take our order! What's with this order excuse anyway?"

190
00:13:22,578 --> 00:13:24,836
"Just go get the food like I told you!"

191
00:13:25,813 --> 00:13:27,623
"Whoa, bestie...

192
00:13:27,623 --> 00:13:29,819
I was just teasing, alright?"

193
00:13:29,819 --> 00:13:31,250
"I mean, look...

194
00:13:31,250 --> 00:13:34,206
you never bring the same person twice!"

195
00:13:34,206 --> 00:13:36,766
"I'm just teasing like usual... that's just how I am!"

196
00:13:36,766 --> 00:13:38,457
"Have I really brought that many people?"

197
00:13:40,728 --> 00:13:41,785
"Want to count on my toes too, bro?"

198
00:13:43,353 --> 00:13:44,228
"Louis...

199
00:13:44,228 --> 00:13:46,087
I'm actually serious about this one. Do you get it?"

200
00:13:46,087 --> 00:13:47,122
"For real? For seal!"

201
00:13:47,122 --> 00:13:48,424
"I'm fucking serious, asshole! Dead serious!

202
00:13:48,424 --> 00:13:49,939
"Okay, okay! You're serious."

203
00:13:49,939 --> 00:13:50,739
"Like... I saw him and I just knew."

204
00:13:50,739 --> 00:13:53,453
"I swear I'm gonna trash this place... Just go get the food already!"

205
00:13:53,453 --> 00:13:55,507
"He's waiting. Don't keep him waiting

206
00:13:57,018 --> 00:13:59,712
"Coming right up! I'll go get your food myself, sir."

207
00:14:08,516 --> 00:14:10,169
"Am I actually gonna get to eat today?"

208
00:14:13,599 --> 00:14:15,144
"Go ahead and order! Whatever you want, just get it!"

209
00:14:15,144 --> 00:14:16,932
"I'm literally starving here!"

210
00:14:33,055 --> 00:14:34,114
Kanghan: "Dig in!"
Time: "Don't mind if I do..."

211
00:14:48,011 --> 00:14:48,744
"Why aren't you eating?

212
00:14:48,744 --> 00:14:50,607
You've just been staring at me."

213
00:14:50,607 --> 00:14:53,563
"Because my heart is already full..."

214
00:14:53,563 --> 00:14:55,949
"Alright, that's way too cheesy!"

215
00:14:55,949 --> 00:14:59,042
"How am I supposed to eat when you're staring like this?"

216
00:15:02,426 --> 00:15:03,886
"Okay, okay! I'll stop staring. Just eat!"

217
00:15:03,886 --> 00:15:05,045
"Back to eating, then..."

218
00:15:21,424 --> 00:15:22,328
"Yes, Dad."

219
00:15:22,328 --> 00:15:25,398
"I'm almost done... I just came out for food with a friend."

220
00:15:25,398 --> 00:15:28,839
"Understood, Dad... I'll head back right away."

221
00:15:28,839 --> 00:15:31,061
"Right, got it, Dad."

222
00:15:31,061 --> 00:15:33,164
"Okay, bye, Dad."

223
00:15:50,670 --> 00:15:51,693
"My dad called."

224
00:15:51,693 --> 00:15:53,523
"Oh, fair enough."

225
00:16:03,376 --> 00:16:04,349
"What's wrong?"

226
00:16:04,349 --> 00:16:06,201
"Why did you get so stressed all of a sudden?"

227
00:16:10,917 --> 00:16:11,741
"Nothing...

228
00:16:11,741 --> 00:16:14,085
"Dad was just asking where I was."

229
00:16:14,085 --> 00:16:15,150
"...and when I'm coming home."

230
00:16:17,833 --> 00:16:19,913
"You're all grown up and you still have a curfew?"

231
00:16:22,041 --> 00:16:22,719
Yeah!

232
00:16:22,719 --> 00:16:25,190
He says I have to be home by 10 PM."

233
00:16:25,190 --> 00:16:28,028
"But today was a special exception."

234
00:16:28,028 --> 00:16:30,307
"Aha!

235
00:16:30,307 --> 00:16:31,758
Is it because you told him you were with me?"

236
00:16:31,758 --> 00:16:33,211
Yeah, right...

237
00:16:33,211 --> 00:16:35,629
If my dad heard that, I'd be dead."

238
00:16:36,456 --> 00:16:37,187
"Why?

239
00:16:37,187 --> 00:16:38,558
Is he really that strict?"

240
00:16:42,455 --> 00:16:45,538
"My dad? He's insanely strict... and a total stickler for rules."

241
00:16:45,538 --> 00:16:50,068
"I have to follow every single rule he sets.            By. The. Book."

242
00:16:50,068 --> 00:16:52,919
"Still, I get it. He means well."

243
00:16:52,919 --> 00:16:57,245
"But sometimes... it's just exhausting."

244
00:16:58,661 --> 00:16:59,656
"No wonder... you take right after your dad."

245
00:17:02,077 --> 00:17:02,929
"Believe it or not...

246
00:17:02,929 --> 00:17:03,868
back then,"

247
00:17:03,868 --> 00:17:06,220
"...I had extra classes until late evening."

248
00:17:06,220 --> 00:17:11,293
"...and as soon as that finished, I had to go straight to swimming at the sports club."

249
00:17:11,293 --> 00:17:13,573
"...and then rush straight back home to study."

250
00:17:13,573 --> 00:17:15,769
"...and be in bed before 10 PM."

251
00:17:15,769 --> 00:17:18,229
"My life was just this endless loop of routines."

252
00:17:18,229 --> 00:17:22,773
"...until I got into university and started interning here."

253
00:17:22,773 --> 00:17:25,684
"Things have slowly gotten better since then."

254
00:17:25,684 --> 00:17:27,781
"Then again..."

255
00:17:27,781 --> 00:17:32,667
"Man... talk about a total silver-spoon lifestyle."

256
00:17:36,948 --> 00:17:39,279
"Alright, alright... I'll stop teasing."

257
00:17:39,279 --> 00:17:42,503
"So... how about your mom? How is she?"

258
00:17:44,155 --> 00:17:46,541
"My mom passed away a long time ago."

259
00:17:46,541 --> 00:17:49,763
"I grew up with just my dad... and Aunt Waew, my nanny."

260
00:17:58,278 --> 00:17:59,968
"Uh... I'm really sorry. I shouldn't have asked."

261
00:17:59,968 --> 00:18:02,151
"It's okay...

262
00:18:02,151 --> 00:18:04,715
my mom passed away before I was even old enough to remember."

263
00:18:04,715 --> 00:18:08,303
"So I ended up growing up with my dad's strict ways."

264
00:18:08,303 --> 00:18:13,331
"I can still remember... the times my dad hit me."

265
00:18:22,317 --> 00:18:23,909
"Anyway... let's just eat."

266
00:18:25,733 --> 00:18:26,465
Okay.

267
00:18:28,983 --> 00:18:30,644
"Earlier, I heard some friends talking about something..."

268
00:18:30,644 --> 00:18:31,275
"Why? What did they say?"

269
00:18:31,275 --> 00:18:34,357
"They were making eyes and giving knowing looks... it totally took me aback."

270
00:18:34,357 --> 00:18:36,110
"They're just making stuff up as usual."

271
00:18:36,110 --> 00:18:39,339
"I don't know what got into him today, talking so much... usually he barely says a word."

272
00:18:39,339 --> 00:18:42,365
"How are you supposed to eat this... spaghetti?"

273
00:19:27,100 --> 00:19:29,700
"Welcome, contestants of 'The Next Leader'!"

274
00:19:36,141 --> 00:19:37,341
"Our 'The Next Leader' program...

275
00:19:37,341 --> 00:19:40,245
is designed to scout the next generation of leaders...

276
00:19:40,245 --> 00:19:43,708
through three main challenges."

277
00:19:43,708 --> 00:19:45,196
"Best of luck to you all."

278
00:19:54,305 --> 00:19:55,837
"Here is the first challenge of the competition."

279
00:19:55,837 --> 00:19:59,102
"Each team must send only one representative."

280
00:19:59,102 --> 00:20:02,991
"Find three leaks within five minutes."

281
00:20:02,991 --> 00:20:04,331
"You may begin!"

282
00:20:36,008 --> 00:20:38,253
"Next, I'd like to invite Team Ya."

283
00:20:39,966 --> 00:20:41,254
"Good luck out there."

284
00:20:47,423 --> 00:20:49,780
"Why is Din so still? He's not doing anything at all..."

285
00:20:49,780 --> 00:20:52,925
"Yeah, true...

286
00:20:52,925 --> 00:20:55,295
He's not even using the equipment.

287
00:20:55,295 --> 00:20:56,806
He's gonna run out of time!"

288
00:21:42,833 --> 00:21:46,324
"Hey! That's a pipe, man, not a patient!"

289
00:21:46,324 --> 00:21:49,354
"Hey Doc... how many months along is your patient?"

290
00:22:31,701 --> 00:22:33,076
"Time is up!"

291
00:22:34,243 --> 00:22:36,280
"Will the technical team please verify the results."

292
00:22:50,407 --> 00:22:52,496
"And the winning team... is...

293
00:22:52,496 --> 00:22:53,978
Team Ya!"

294
00:23:01,781 --> 00:23:03,898
"You... you were incredible!"

295
00:23:03,898 --> 00:23:06,295
"How did you do that... do you have super hearing?"

296
00:23:06,295 --> 00:23:07,726
Not really...

297
00:23:08,697 --> 00:23:10,036
"just a special skill."

298
00:23:10,036 --> 00:23:13,905
"My dad taught me...my ears are really sensitive to the sound of water."

299
00:23:13,905 --> 00:23:16,243
"You... are truly incredible."

300
00:23:36,568 --> 00:23:38,207
"Mr. Itthikorn is currently with a guest and isn't available to meet."

301
00:23:43,151 --> 00:23:46,374
"I left a folder in the room... Could you grab it for me, please? It's for my dad."

302
00:23:46,374 --> 00:23:47,274
"Of course."

303
00:23:50,108 --> 00:23:51,196
"Ya is certainly impressive...

304
00:23:51,196 --> 00:23:53,934
and that Din guy is no slacker either."

305
00:23:53,934 --> 00:23:57,905
"But it's only the first challenge...

306
00:23:57,905 --> 00:24:00,289
Your daughter didn't even do anything."

307
00:24:00,289 --> 00:24:05,236
"I think you're being a bit too hasty... Just get straight to the point."

308
00:24:05,236 --> 00:24:07,194
"Then I won't beat around the bush."

309
00:24:07,194 --> 00:24:11,714
"The foreign investors won't wait for us much longer."

310
00:24:11,714 --> 00:24:14,912
"You know very well... that I never agreed to this."

311
00:24:14,912 --> 00:24:17,882
"How long are you going to keep being this stubborn?"

312
00:24:17,882 --> 00:24:21,865
They're just your interns—a bunch of hicks.

313
00:24:21,865 --> 00:24:30,561
Our company could grow so much more with foreign executives on board.

314
00:24:30,561 --> 00:24:31,687
You know that."

315
00:24:31,687 --> 00:24:33,577
"This is my company...

316
00:24:33,577 --> 00:24:35,537
I built it with my own hands."

317
00:24:37,727 --> 00:24:38,803
"Fine...

318
00:24:38,803 --> 00:24:42,700
I'll play along with your game for now."

319
00:24:46,351 --> 00:24:47,843
"But don't forget our deal...

320
00:24:47,843 --> 00:24:54,644
If my team wins, the chairmanship is mine."

321
00:25:22,679 --> 00:25:24,091
"Here's some coffee."

322
00:25:24,091 --> 00:25:25,880
"What are you working on?"

323
00:25:25,880 --> 00:25:33,040
"You don't look like someone who just won at all."

324
00:25:37,094 --> 00:25:38,938
"Thanks."

325
00:25:38,938 --> 00:25:42,415
"Don't get too attached to success...

326
00:25:42,415 --> 00:25:44,620
It'll pass soon enough."

327
00:25:45,801 --> 00:25:50,970
"Come on, man... can you just enjoy the victory for once?"

328
00:25:53,009 --> 00:25:54,525
"I mean, I always knew you were going to win anyway."

329
00:25:54,525 --> 00:25:58,516
"You're our company's 'Golden-Eared Din', man!"

330
00:25:59,841 --> 00:26:00,771
"What 'golden ears'?

331
00:26:00,771 --> 00:26:02,170
"People are just talking nonsense."

332
00:26:04,841 --> 00:26:06,025
"Take this, for example."

333
00:26:06,025 --> 00:26:07,856
"Like that time you came over to my place..."

334
00:26:07,856 --> 00:26:10,042
"You listened to the water for a second, and then—click..."

335
00:26:10,042 --> 00:26:11,943
"Just like that, you already knew exactly where the leak was."

336
00:26:11,943 --> 00:26:16,479
"Otherwise, my water bill would've cost me a fortune!"

337
00:26:16,479 --> 00:26:21,829
"If you actually bothered to check your water meter... and saw it spinning nonstop..."

338
00:26:21,829 --> 00:26:23,881
"...you'd know there's a leak somewhere."

339
00:26:23,881 --> 00:26:26,358
"If you were just a little more observant..."

340
00:26:26,358 --> 00:26:28,004
"...that's all it takes."

341
00:26:31,254 --> 00:26:32,373
"As you command, Master..."

342
00:26:33,337 --> 00:26:35,273
"Oh, so you're mocking me now?"

343
00:26:35,273 --> 00:26:36,714
"Whoa!!"

344
00:26:40,336 --> 00:26:41,600
"Woah, take it easy, man!"

345
00:26:41,600 --> 00:26:46,743
"Seriously though, you need to stop overthinking and taking everything so seriously."

346
00:26:48,293 --> 00:26:49,818
"Even my mom tells me,

347
00:26:49,818 --> 00:26:53,075
'Why can't you be more like Din?'"

348
00:26:53,075 --> 00:26:54,666
"'Do this, do that!'"

349
00:27:01,625 --> 00:27:02,595
"But jokes aside..."

350
00:27:02,595 --> 00:27:05,731
"I never really thought... you'd actually help Ya."

351
00:27:13,582 --> 00:27:14,372
"Look at you, getting all flustered..."

352
00:27:14,372 --> 00:27:17,374
"Seriously though...

353
00:27:17,374 --> 00:27:19,255
do you have a crush on Ya?"

354
00:27:22,081 --> 00:27:24,673
"That's crazy... Who'd even think of something like that?"

355
00:27:24,673 --> 00:27:26,130
"Riiiight... It's just us, man.

356
00:27:26,130 --> 00:27:27,961
You can tell me."

357
00:27:27,961 --> 00:27:29,551
"Come on, it's me!"

358
00:27:29,551 --> 00:27:33,576
"We've known each other way too long. I can see right through you."

359
00:27:33,576 --> 00:27:35,808
"So... do you like her like that?"

360
00:27:39,495 --> 00:27:41,835
"Look, man...

361
00:27:41,835 --> 00:27:45,525
when you like someone, you gotta make a move.

362
00:27:45,525 --> 00:27:46,507
Got it?"

363
00:27:46,507 --> 00:27:49,682
"Otherwise... Ya is drop-dead gorgeous.

364
00:27:49,682 --> 00:27:51,520
Someone at the office will snatch her up!"

365
00:28:00,742 --> 00:28:02,005
"Like how you're going after Time?"

366
00:28:04,617 --> 00:28:05,278
"Wait... you knew about that?"

367
00:28:05,278 --> 00:28:07,830
"Wow... you can see that from Mars!"

368
00:28:07,830 --> 00:28:09,335
"Pretty sure the whole office knows by now."

369
00:28:11,658 --> 00:28:12,749
"I had no idea...

370
00:28:12,749 --> 00:28:14,377
I was actually making a move on Time."

371
00:28:17,115 --> 00:28:20,524
"Woah... no way... Was it really that obvious?"

372
00:28:23,615 --> 00:28:24,566
"I knew it, man... God,

373
00:28:24,566 --> 00:28:27,983
I miss Young Master Time so much."

374
00:28:27,983 --> 00:28:30,898
"If you'll excuse me, I'm off to see my love."

375
00:28:30,898 --> 00:28:32,776
"Off you go!"

376
00:28:32,776 --> 00:28:34,534
"Catch you later!"

377
00:28:37,404 --> 00:28:38,886
Sighs... Young Master Time.

378
00:28:59,943 --> 00:29:02,881
"Aha! Shooting a music video out here?"

379
00:29:05,276 --> 00:29:06,534
"Normally, around this time..."

380
00:29:06,534 --> 00:29:10,210
"I'd usually be at tutoring... or swimming at the sports club."

381
00:29:10,210 --> 00:29:12,787
"And after that, I'd rush home...

382
00:29:12,787 --> 00:29:14,980
right as it got dark."

383
00:29:14,980 --> 00:29:17,905
"Believe it or not...

384
00:29:17,905 --> 00:29:20,750
I hardly ever got to see this time of day."

385
00:29:20,750 --> 00:29:23,769
"Why are you getting so dramatic all of a sudden?"

386
00:29:25,981 --> 00:29:27,041
"But seriously though..."

387
00:29:27,041 --> 00:29:30,760
"And I barely even had any friends back then."

388
00:29:30,760 --> 00:29:34,812
"As for close friends... I could count them on one hand."

389
00:29:34,812 --> 00:29:40,553
"Thanks a lot... for listening to me ramble like this."

390
00:29:50,187 --> 00:29:51,283
"Are you sick or something?"

391
00:29:53,811 --> 00:29:54,903
"Don't be silly... I'm not."

392
00:29:59,144 --> 00:30:03,424
"I just feel good... having you around."

393
00:30:09,684 --> 00:30:10,345
"Time...

394
00:30:10,345 --> 00:30:12,246
saying stuff like that is gonna make me blush."

395
00:30:12,246 --> 00:30:13,733
"Normally,

396
00:30:13,733 --> 00:30:15,831
you'd practically be at my throat."

397
00:30:15,831 --> 00:30:18,375
"Seriously, you've gotta be coming down with something today."

398
00:30:18,375 --> 00:30:20,935
"See? Even your ears are turning red."

399
00:30:24,224 --> 00:30:25,599
"Yep, that proves it!"

400
00:30:25,599 --> 00:30:26,974
"What?"

401
00:30:26,974 --> 00:30:27,474
"So you really are sick, huh?"

402
00:30:27,474 --> 00:30:29,111
"Why are you being so sweet all of a sudden?"

403
00:30:36,347 --> 00:30:38,057
"Wait... are you actually taking the competition that seriously?"

404
00:30:42,347 --> 00:30:47,538
"Come on... we've got Din, Ya, you, and me."

405
00:30:47,538 --> 00:30:49,688
"We're basically a dream team."

406
00:30:49,688 --> 00:30:54,097
"Either way... we're definitely winning the next round."

407
00:30:54,097 --> 00:30:55,887
"Just trust me."

408
00:31:04,219 --> 00:31:05,677
"Time...

409
00:31:07,343 --> 00:31:08,876
don't worry.

410
00:31:08,876 --> 00:31:15,496
You've still got me. I promise I'll take care of you."

411
00:31:39,964 --> 00:31:42,453
"Ah... nice weather today, huh?"

412
00:32:22,542 --> 00:32:23,397
Oh, hey

413
00:32:23,397 --> 00:32:25,484
thanks.

414
00:32:26,833 --> 00:32:28,289
"Thanks so much for today.

415
00:32:28,289 --> 00:32:30,598
Without you, our team would've been in big trouble."

416
00:32:32,582 --> 00:32:34,319
"Since I promised I'd compete,

417
00:32:34,319 --> 00:32:35,996
I'm giving it my all."

418
00:32:35,996 --> 00:32:38,005
"I know how serious you are."

419
00:32:38,005 --> 00:32:39,987
"I just hope you take this seriously, too."

420
00:32:39,987 --> 00:32:43,675
"Am I not taking this seriously enough?

421
00:32:43,675 --> 00:32:45,862
I can't afford to lose this match either."

422
00:32:46,956 --> 00:32:50,182
"Even if you lose... you've still got a safety net, right?"

423
00:32:50,182 --> 00:32:51,618
"What do you even have to struggle with?"

424
00:32:52,747 --> 00:32:54,579
"Just stop saying that."

425
00:32:54,579 --> 00:32:57,777
"I just found out that if I lose...

426
00:32:57,777 --> 00:33:00,059
my dad will be removed as chairman."

427
00:33:01,745 --> 00:33:02,460
"Are you serious?...

428
00:33:03,828 --> 00:33:04,984
How did you find out?"

429
00:33:04,984 --> 00:33:08,690
"I overheard Uncle Ronnayuth talking to my dad."

430
00:33:14,660 --> 00:33:15,619
"So in the end...

431
00:33:15,619 --> 00:33:19,039
we're just pawns for rich people to play with?"

432
00:33:20,410 --> 00:33:23,753
"Don't jump to conclusions just yet. We don't even know the whole story."

433
00:33:23,753 --> 00:33:28,222
"Honestly, my dad wouldn't gamble with the company like this."

434
00:33:28,222 --> 00:33:32,211
"But isn't he your uncle, though? They're all family, after all."

435
00:33:32,211 --> 00:33:33,833
"It's always family that's the worst."

436
00:33:33,833 --> 00:33:36,362
"And he's family... What kind of relative does something like this?"

437
00:33:36,362 --> 00:33:39,722
"Even knowing I was competing, he still sabotaged me like this."

438
00:33:39,722 --> 00:33:42,528
"I guess he was never really sincere with me."

439
00:33:42,528 --> 00:33:44,791
"My dad and uncle don't really get along, either."

440
00:33:47,739 --> 00:33:48,367
"Then...

441
00:33:50,864 --> 00:33:52,049
do you actually mean well by me?"

442
00:33:52,049 --> 00:33:54,555
"Well, what do you think?"

443
00:33:54,555 --> 00:33:59,781
"You've been so good to me... rest assured, I'm in this fight with you."

444
00:34:03,029 --> 00:34:05,550
"Then... we fight together...

445
00:34:05,550 --> 00:34:07,048
and we win together."

446
00:34:07,048 --> 00:34:07,548
"Yeah."

447
00:34:07,548 --> 00:34:08,844
"Are you okay?"

448
00:34:08,844 --> 00:34:11,295
"Thank you."

449
00:35:19,769 --> 00:35:22,682
"Didn't you set up 'The Next Leader' just for Ya, brother?"

450
00:35:22,682 --> 00:35:25,183
"That's right... I set it up just for Ya."

451
00:35:25,183 --> 00:35:29,075
"And besides, I also created it to develop my employees."

452
00:35:29,075 --> 00:35:31,624
"What a waste of time, brother. Why even bother?"

453
00:35:31,624 --> 00:35:34,408
"See? That's where you and I are different."

454
00:35:34,408 --> 00:35:39,198
"If we brought in foreign joint ventures, our company would go so much further."

455
00:35:39,198 --> 00:35:43,225
"No! Not as long as I'm still the president here."

456
00:35:43,225 --> 00:35:44,535
"Not a chance!"

457
00:35:59,847 --> 00:36:01,808
"Because... I want to be more than just friends."

458
00:36:01,808 --> 00:36:03,889
"What did you mean by that?"

459
00:36:03,889 --> 00:36:05,641
"I'm going to need everyone's help today."

460
00:36:05,641 --> 00:36:07,374
"No problem at all, bro."

461
00:36:07,374 --> 00:36:11,252
"Next, here is the challenge for Round 2."

462
00:36:11,252 --> 00:36:14,329
"Everyone... I've got an idea."

463
00:36:15,929 --> 00:36:17,352
"Why does their idea sound exactly like ours?"

464
00:36:17,352 --> 00:36:19,567
"Did those bastards cheat or what?"
"Hell yeah."

465
00:36:19,567 --> 00:36:23,275
"In the real world... simplicity isn't what counts."

466
00:36:23,275 --> 00:36:26,078
"Someone like you will never become a leader."

467
00:36:26,078 --> 00:36:30,975
"Someday, you'll understand why I did what I did."

468
00:36:30,975 --> 00:36:35,433
"But honestly... I really hate seeing you like this."
